# BusyBox init fallback for images without systemd (target image).
#
# Append the respawn line to /etc/inittab. BusyBox init re-runs the command
# whenever it exits, which is the equivalent of systemd's Restart=always for
# this one service. `run` execs the supervisor in the foreground (and records
# its PID), so PID 1 supervises the real process.
#
# Only ONE thyme supervisor may run per image: either use this line or start
# it from rcS (/etc/init.d/thyme-app start), never both. With respawn active,
# `stop` cannot defeat PID 1; for maintenance comment the line out and
# `kill -HUP 1`, then run /etc/init.d/thyme-app stop.
#
# No watchdog here: BusyBox init only notices process death. Role stalls are
# still covered by OPS-01 inside the supervisor, and a hung supervisor is
# caught by the health endpoint from external monitoring (OPS-10).

# -- thyme supervisor (respawn on exit) --------------------------------------
::respawn:/etc/init.d/thyme-app run
::shutdown:/etc/init.d/thyme-app stop
